{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21451 - PROTEIN:5782",
  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside is implicated in the interaction with DMS-273 through a series of molecular pathways involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a target for multiple compounds, including 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)-, both of which are linked to DMS-273. The evidence suggests that Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may act as a modulator of the proteasome pathway, potentially influencing the activity of these compounds in the context of DMS-273. The shared involvement of the 26S proteasome in the targets of these compounds implies a possible mechanism by which Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside could affect DMS-273, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the proteasome in mediating the effects of these compounds on DMS-273, underscoring the importance of this subunit in the biological response to these molecules.",
